// Failures grouped by result code and route.
//
// Split by resultCode rather than lumping all failures together, because the codes mean very
// different things here. A 404 from /api/books/{id} is the API behaving correctly for a missing
// row. A 500 is a defect. A 503 usually means the platform, not the code - an instance recycling
// or the database still resuming.
requests
| where timestamp > ago(24h)
| where success == false
| summarize count() by resultCode, name
| order by count_ desc
